__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# ⛔ WHITELIST, NOT A DENYLIST — measured 2026-09-07, and this file is why.
# It read `data/*.jsonl` plus `data/*.counters.json`: one pattern per sidecar, enumerated
# by name. Adding the refusals sidecar (`5ebd805`) created a THIRD name matching neither,
# so `records.jsonl.refusals.json` was tracked and rode into SIX consecutive commits of a
# PUBLIC repo, bumping its counter in each. Nothing private escaped — the step was a probe
# named "nope" — but a refusal records the CONSUMER's step name, and the next real one
# would have published it. A denylist of runtime state is wrong the moment state is added,
# and it fails silently, in the direction that publishes.
# `sjv` already had this right; this is that pattern adopted rather than reinvented.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
